Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: WebKitGTK
Upstream-Contact: https://webkitgtk.org/
Source: https://webkitgtk.org/releases/
Comment: A build of upstream WebKitGTK with the downstream patches in patches/ of the
 amber-webkit source package applied, if there are any; each patch's header says what it
 changes. Corresponding source for this build: the release tarball
 https://webkitgtk.org/releases/webkitgtk-2.54.1.tar.xz plus those patches. The libraries
 are shipped as separate, dynamically linked shared objects under the private path
 /usr/lib/amber-webkit/, so the LGPL's shared-library terms apply.
 .
 The stanzas below follow the licence files in the tarball, one per part of the source
 that is compiled into what these packages ship. Parts that are not built or not shipped
 (the test suites, the Web Inspector's external libraries, gtest, the sysprof capture
 library, the Windows and Android support code) are not listed.

